  "title": "Zaragoza: combining awareness raising and financial measures to enhance water efficiency",
  "summary": "The Zaragoza Water Saving City program combines awareness campaigns with financial measures to enhance water efficiency. By involving stakeholders, coordinating efforts, targeting sectors, and gaining political commitment, Zaragoza achieved a nearly 30% reduction in water consumption. However, economic constraints have slowed further progress. The Zaragoza Water Saving City programme was initiated in 1996 in response to water scarcity and is still on-going. It has included awareness raising campaigns, the implementation of examples of good practice of reduced water consumption and voluntary public commitments by citizens and businesses.",
